@@ Module conventions
-- [tool.uv] package = false, with the check runner injecting PYTHONPATH=<root>/src.
-  Avoids a build backend and the wheel-packages array that silently drops a module.
+- For a repository whose CALL requires installation, use one installable
+  src/<package>/ root with a pinned native build backend; run checks against
+  its uv-synced installation. Keep package=false/PYTHONPATH only for a
+  deliberately non-distributed script repository.
@@ Test layout
-- pythonpath = ["src"] makes that work without installing the project.
+- Installable projects verify the built wheel from a separate environment
+  outside the checkout without PYTHONPATH; import smoke is not user acceptance.
+- tests/tools may mirror development-only tools/ outside the shipped package.
@@ Known landmines
+- Windows subprocess text capture must set encoding="utf-8" and require UTF-8
+  from the child, rather than decoding tool output with the Windows locale.
Evidence: docs/setup/evidence/check-initial.txt and install-probe.txt.
